From an ecological standpoint, ants serve vital roles as decomposers, soil aerators, and predators that sustain ecosystem balance. Yet from a philosophical perspective, ants possess no inherent or teleological purpose; like all living things, they simply exist, reproduce, and perish according to the blind mechanisms of natural selection. Any "purpose" we attribute to them is ultimately a human projection onto a creature that merely *is*, fulfilling its niche without destiny or design.
